/T (TagWraps sets lock bits on all user memory pages after writing the signature data. The chip UID is in factory-set read-only memory and was never writable. The result is a chip that any NFC device can read but no device can modify by any means short of physical destruction. A counterfeiter who recovers a chip from a discarded genuine product cannot reuse it. They cannot clear the existing signature data and write their own, nor can they alter the product information stored in user memory.)
/E (TagWraps sets lock bits on all user memory pages after writing the signature data. The chip UID is in factory-set read-only memory and was never writable. The result is a chip that any NFC device can read but no device can modify by any means short of physical destruction. A counterfeiter who recovers a chip from a discarded genuine product cannot reuse it. They cannot clear the existing signature data and write their own, nor can they alter the product information stored in user memory.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [12]
